us two test rows; batch it into the commit Chunk 08 already plans, or accept and record it.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Canvas/OutlineGrammar.cs", "src/Cordyceps.Tests/ObjectResolverTests.cs"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "status prints name \"\" for a parameter object whose nickname is empty", "recommendation": "instance: ActionStatus keeps the component-era expression name = obj.NickName != obj.Name ? obj.NickName : obj.Name. A component never has an empty nickname, but the population now includes sliders and panels, whose nickname is empty until someone sets one (the resolver already treats empty nicknames as a real case). For those the expression yields the empty string, not the type name. The entry shape is unchanged, but the value is blank for the most common new entries. Not verifiable from code alone: confirm the default NickName of a new Number Slider and Panel in the live host (VRF-019/021 are being rewritten in Chunk 08). If confirmed, fall back to obj.Name when the nickname is empty. Boundary rating would be WARNING if confirmed. Priced: one condition; batch into Chunk 08's commit or accept.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Tools/Unified/GhInspectTool.cs"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "ResolveIntent's comment says removal lookups take the intent with no default; the single lookups have intent-less overloads", "recommendation": "instance: the enum summary in ObjectResolver.cs reads 'The lookups a removal action uses take it with no default, so a new removal action cannot forget to decide.' That is true of ToolHelpers.ResolveIds only. TryGetUnprotectedComponent, TryGetUnprotectedComponentWithDoc, TryGetUnprotectedObject and TryGetUnprotectedGroup each keep an overload without intent that means Ordinary, and three of the four removal actions (group_delete, gh_wire clear, gh_wire disconnect) use single lookups. The plan's mid-build decision records this shape, so the code is as decided; the comment is the