d the Objects-scope group hint still offers that name", "recommendation": "instance: the outline ActionInfo tip lists why an object or group prints as an id (edge spaces, separators, leading marks, ']') but not the case commit 4602301 added (a group carrying the default name 'Group'), nor the older one (an object with a default nickname). An agent loses nothing: the id it sees works everywhere. Related: under destructive intent, delete id='Group' answers ''Group' is a group; group actions take its name, ...', and group_delete then refuses that name; the hint already prints the id, so the caller recovers in one more turn. Priced: NOTE at the boundary; one clause in the tip if the help text is touched again, else accept.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Tools/Unified/GhCanvasTool.Outline.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/Canvas/ObjectResolver.cs"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Outline's 'N objects' and status's summary.total count different sets", "recommendation": "none (no defect to bound): error, warning and disconnected counts now agree object for object (ObjectHealth.IsSubject on both sides; ObjectHealthTests.StatusPopulation_MatchesOutline pins it). The totals do not: outline's summary counts every canvas node, scribbles and sketches included (the test's own fixture reads '6 objects' against 5 listed), while status counts subjects only. The plan's inference says 'its counts and outline's agree'; say in the Chunk 08 documentation which counts are meant. Priced: accept; a sentence in the guide Chunk 08 is already rewriting.", "files": ["src/Cordyceps/Core/Canvas/OutlineView.cs"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "OutlineGrammar says OutlineView builds its lines from its constants; six sites still use literals", "recommendation": "instance: OutlineView.cs still joins with the literal \" \u00b7 \" at the summary, group line, ungrouped line and network text, writes \" = \" in InputRef and \" (\" / \"; \" in several refs. The strin